      "dom_id": "question-67314",
      "name": null,
      "problem": "The eighth and ninth terms of an arithmetic sequence are $65$ and $73,$ respectively. Determine the formula for the $n$th term of the sequence.",
      "worked_solution": "The formula for the $n$th term is given by  \n\n$$\n{a}_{n}={a}_{1}+(n-1)d,\n$$\n\nso we need to figure out the first term ${a}_{1}$ and the common difference $d.$\n\nSince the terms ${a}_{8}=65$ and ${a}_{9}=73$ are consecutive, we can subtract them to find the common difference:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & ={a}_{9}-{a}_{8} \\\\  & =73-65 \\\\  & =8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can use one of our known values, say, ${a}_{8}=65,$ to determine the first term of the sequence. Since ${a}_{8}$ is $7$ jumps after ${a}_{1},$ we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{8} & ={a}_{1}+7d \\\\ 65 & ={a}_{1}+7\\cdot 8 \\\\ 65 & ={a}_{1}+56 \\\\ 65-56 & ={a}_{1} \\\\ {a}_{1} & =9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo the formula for the $n$th term of this arithmetic sequence is:  \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{n} & ={a}_{1}+(n-1)d \\\\  & =9+(n-1)\\cdot 8 \\\\  & =9+8n-8 \\\\  & =8n+1\\end{aligned}\n$$",
