    {
      "dom_id": "question-177690",
      "name": null,
      "problem": "The $9$th and $10$th terms of an arithmetic sequence are $49$ and $45,$ respectively. Determine the formula for the $n$th term of the sequence.",
      "worked_solution": "The formula for the $n$th term is given by \n\n$$\n{a}_{n}={a}_{1}+(n-1)d,\n$$\n\nso we need to figure out the first term ${a}_{1}$ and the common difference $d.$ \n\nSince the terms ${a}_{9}=49$ and ${a}_{10}=45$ are consecutive, we can subtract them to find the common difference:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & ={a}_{10}-{a}_{9} \\\\  & =45-49 \\\\  & =-4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can use one of our known values, say, ${a}_{9}=49,$ to determine the first term of the sequence. Since ${a}_{9}$ is $8$ jumps after ${a}_{1},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{9} & ={a}_{1}+8d \\\\ 49 & ={a}_{1}+8(-4) \\\\ 49 & ={a}_{1}-32 \\\\ 49+32 & ={a}_{1} \\\\ {a}_{1} & =81.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the formula for the $n$th term of this arithmetic sequence is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{n} & ={a}_{1}+(n-1)d \\\\  & =81+(n-1)(-4) \\\\  & =81-4n+4 \\\\  & =85-4n.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
